{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_53","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"artifactsRead\":[\"convex/_generated/ai/guidelines.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/02-finalization-boundary-between-live-state-and-archive.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/provider-adapter.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts\",\"convex/processHistoryItems.ts\",\"tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts\",\"tests/service/server/process-live-updates.test.ts\",\"tests/service/client/process-live.test.ts\",\"tests/service/client/archive-section.test.ts\",\"tests/fixtures/archive.ts\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Reviewed Story 2 against its story/spec/test-plan, then verified the finalization seam across `ArchiveFinalizationService`, the user-response and execution hooks, process-history compatibility, and the Story 2 server/client tests. I also ran the configured story and epic gates plus an ad hoc runtime reproduction of execution-result archiving.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"story-02-history-bridge-identity-mismatch\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Execution-result archive rows are keyed to transient provider IDs instead of the persisted live history items\",\"evidence\":\"`ProcessEnvironmentService.applyExecutionResultSideEffects` persists each execution history item first, but then calls `appendFromProcessHistoryItem` with the original provider payload instead of the stored row (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:690-706`). `ArchiveFinalizationService.appendFromProcessHistoryItem` derives `sourceObjectId` and `finalizationKey` directly from `historyItem.historyItemId` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts:57-93`). Both the in-memory store and the real Convex mutation generate fresh history IDs/createdAt values when appending history (`apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3144-3153`, `convex/processHistoryItems.ts:93-119`). An ad hoc reproduction returned `storedHistoryIds` `[\\\"pr:history-process_message-1\\\"]` while the archive entry used `sourceObjectId` `\\\"runtime-model-1\\\"` and `finalizationKey` `\\\"model:runtime-model-1\\\"`. That means the canonical archive is not actually bridged from the persisted current-history row, and later history-based reconciliation would target a different identity. The current TC-2.3b test encodes the transient provider ID instead of checking the stored history row (`tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts:252-257`).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\",\"tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.3\",\"TC-2.3a\",\"TC-2.3b\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"story-02-history-bridge-identity-mismatch\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Execution-result archive rows are keyed to transient provider IDs instead of the persisted live history items\",\"evidence\":\"`ProcessEnvironmentService.applyExecutionResultSideEffects` persists each execution history item first, but then calls `appendFromProcessHistoryItem` with the original provider payload instead of the stored row (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:690-706`). `ArchiveFinalizationService.appendFromProcessHistoryItem` derives `sourceObjectId` and `finalizationKey` directly from `historyItem.historyItemId` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts:57-93`). Both the in-memory store and the real Convex mutation generate fresh history IDs/createdAt values when appending history (`apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3144-3153`, `convex/processHistoryItems.ts:93-119`). An ad hoc reproduction returned `storedHistoryIds` `[\\\"pr:history-process_message-1\\\"]` while the archive entry used `sourceObjectId` `\\\"runtime-model-1\\\"` and `finalizationKey` `\\\"model:runtime-model-1\\\"`. That means the canonical archive is not actually bridged from the persisted current-history row, and later history-based reconciliation would target a different identity. The current TC-2.3b test encodes the transient provider ID instead of checking the stored history row (`tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts:252-257`).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\",\"tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.3\",\"TC-2.3a\",\"TC-2.3b\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-2.1\",\"TC-2.1a\",\"AC-2.2\",\"TC-2.2a\",\"TC-2.2b\"],\"unverified\":[\"AC-2.3\",\"TC-2.3a\",\"TC-2.3b\"]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run test:service -- --run tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run green-verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"The real execution-result hook archives the pre-persistence provider object instead of the persisted `processHistoryItems` row, so production archive identity diverges from the live-history identity even though duplicate suppression still passes.\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"revise\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"openQuestions\":[],\"additionalObservations\":[\"`green-verify` and `verify-all` both passed, but the current Story 2 tests miss the identity mismatch because TC-2.3b asserts the provider-supplied `runtime-model-1` ID rather than the stored history row returned by `appendProcessHistoryItem`.\",\"Live/archive separation itself is otherwise evidenced well: `tests/service/server/process-live-updates.test.ts:306-372` and `tests/service/client/process-live.test.ts:243-274` both show websocket/reducer history upserts do not create archive rows.\",\"I did not find a fake adapter or placeholder branch wired into the runtime finalization path; the blocking issue is a real production data-link mismatch in the execution completion hook.\"]}"}}
